1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,532
Welcome to the automation module!

2
00:00:02,532 --> 00:00:06,103
Before we build anything, let's
learn how workflows think.

3
00:00:06,103 --> 00:00:10,598
Once you understand three simple ideas,
triggers, actions and conditions,

4
00:00:10,598 --> 00:00:15,031
you'll be able to read any workflow,
and build your own with confidence.

5
00:00:15,887 --> 00:00:18,855
Workflows live under
Automation, in the sidebar.

6
00:00:18,855 --> 00:00:20,896
Here's the list for Bloom Dental.

7
00:00:20,896 --> 00:00:25,780
You can group workflows into folders,
and for each one you can see whether it's

8
00:00:25,780 --> 00:00:29,861
published or still a draft, and
how many contacts it has enrolled.

9
00:00:30,716 --> 00:00:35,791
Let's open the Lead Nurture folder, and
look at the workflow that follows up every

10
00:00:35,791 --> 00:00:37,029
new Invisalign lead.

11
00:00:37,029 --> 00:00:41,114
Reading a real one is the fastest
way to understand how they work.

12
00:00:41,965 --> 00:00:44,239
Every workflow starts with a trigger.

13
00:00:44,239 --> 00:00:48,601
The trigger is the when: the event
that adds a contact to the workflow.

14
00:00:48,601 --> 00:00:50,199
This one has two triggers.

15
00:00:50,199 --> 00:00:53,333
A contact enters when they
submit the website form,

16
00:00:53,333 --> 00:00:55,914
or when they fill in a Facebook lead form.

17
00:00:55,914 --> 00:00:57,204
Either one is enough.

18
00:00:58,053 --> 00:01:00,019
Triggers usually have filters.

19
00:01:00,019 --> 00:01:01,855
Click a trigger to see them.

20
00:01:01,855 --> 00:01:04,804
This filter says: form
is Invisalign Enquiry.

21
00:01:04,804 --> 00:01:07,360
So only that form starts this workflow.

22
00:01:07,360 --> 00:01:11,489
Someone filling in your general
contact form won't be enrolled.

23
00:01:11,489 --> 00:01:16,077
Filters are how you make sure the
right people get the right messages.

24
00:01:16,928 --> 00:01:19,187
Under the trigger come the actions.

25
00:01:19,187 --> 00:01:23,575
Actions are the what: everything
the workflow does for that contact.

26
00:01:23,575 --> 00:01:25,381
They run from top to bottom.

27
00:01:25,381 --> 00:01:30,738
Here, Kyntlo creates an opportunity in the
pipeline, sends an instant text message,

28
00:01:30,738 --> 00:01:33,964
and notifies the team
member assigned to the lead.

29
00:01:33,964 --> 00:01:36,997
All within seconds of
the form being submitted.

30
00:01:37,848 --> 00:01:38,838
Next is a wait.

31
00:01:38,838 --> 00:01:44,382
A wait pauses the contact right here, in
this case for one day, before they move on.

32
00:01:44,382 --> 00:01:49,133
Waits are what turn a single message
into a friendly follow-up sequence,

33
00:01:49,133 --> 00:01:51,905
instead of five messages arriving at once.

34
00:01:52,754 --> 00:01:54,277
Then comes a condition.

35
00:01:54,277 --> 00:01:59,375
This If/Else step asks a question: has
the contact booked a consultation yet?

36
00:01:59,375 --> 00:02:02,222
Contacts who have, go
down the Booked path.

37
00:02:02,222 --> 00:02:07,585
Everyone else goes down the None path,
and gets a gentle email and one more text.

38
00:02:07,585 --> 00:02:10,234
Each contact only ever travels one path.

39
00:02:11,088 --> 00:02:12,375
Here's the key idea.

40
00:02:12,375 --> 00:02:15,272
A workflow runs separately
for every contact.

41
00:02:15,272 --> 00:02:20,485
Olivia might be waiting on day one, while
Sophie has already booked and finished.

42
00:02:20,485 --> 00:02:25,377
You can see exactly who's in the workflow,
and where, in Enrollment History.

43
00:02:26,226 --> 00:02:28,394
Finally, the switch at the top right.

44
00:02:28,394 --> 00:02:30,797
A workflow only runs when it's published.

45
00:02:30,797 --> 00:02:34,958
While it's a draft, you can build
and test safely, and nothing is sent.

46
00:02:34,958 --> 00:02:38,240
When you're happy, switch it
to Publish, and click Save.

47
00:02:39,091 --> 00:02:42,994
Workflow automation is included
on the Growth and Pro plans.

48
00:02:42,994 --> 00:02:48,134
A handful of premium actions, like Google
Sheets and custom webhooks, need Pro,

49
00:02:48,134 --> 00:02:50,931
and we'll cover those
later in this module.

50
00:02:51,780 --> 00:02:52,824
Here's a pro tip.

51
00:02:52,824 --> 00:02:56,261
Before you build, describe
the workflow in one sentence.

52
00:02:56,261 --> 00:03:00,128
When someone submits the Invisalign
form, text them right away,

53
00:03:00,128 --> 00:03:03,197
and if they haven't booked
after a day, follow up.

54
00:03:03,197 --> 00:03:08,292
The when is your trigger, the do is your
actions, and the unless is your condition.

55
00:03:09,140 --> 00:03:11,099
Now you know how workflows think.

56
00:03:11,099 --> 00:03:15,967
In the next lesson, we'll build your first
one from scratch, a new lead follow-up,

57
00:03:15,967 --> 00:03:17,867
and test it before it goes live.

58
00:03:17,867 --> 00:03:18,698
See you there!
